60:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
61:    """
62:    Sort the 5x5 marker fragments into the 3x3 slots indicated by their orientations and complete any missing symmetric fragments.
63:
64:    Input structure
65:    The grid is a 19x19 canvas split by black separator rows and columns into a 3x3 array of 5x5 tiles.
66:    Inside the tiles there are exactly two nonblack colors: a frequent fill color and a less frequent marker color.
67:    Nonblank marker masks are fragments whose centroid direction relative to the 5x5 center names one of the nine slots.
68:
69:    Rule
70:    Classify each nonblank marker mask by the signs of its row and column offsets from the tile center: top/center/bottom and left/center/right.
71:    For every output slot, collect all dihedral symmetries of the known fragments that would land in that slot, assert they agree, and use that mask.
72:    Rebuild the same separated 3x3 tile canvas with each completed mask in its classified slot.
73:
74:    Key insight
75:    The input is a shuffled library of symmetric tile fragments; each fragment's centroid direction is its target position.
76:    """
